# Installed scripts: the Marketplace tab OUT OF THE BOX. No `# env:`
# line, no config, no `MNML_SCRIPTS_MARKETPLACE` — the curated set is
# mnml's own `lua/` folder, found beside the binary (or baked in from
# the checkout it was built from), exactly the way the official
# integrations live in `integrations/`. This file is the acceptance for
# that: a fresh run lists the five shipped scripts and says nothing
# about a repo that does not exist.
command view.activity_scripts
expect screen contains "SCRIPTS"
expect screen contains "Mkt (5)"
command script.show_marketplace
expect screen contains "eslint"
expect screen contains "git-blame-line"
expect screen contains "recent-commands"
expect screen contains "surround-word"
expect screen contains "todo-list"
# The badge is `✓ Official`, clipped to the tree's width at the shipped
# `tree_width = 30`.
expect screen contains "Offi"
# The dead "not live yet" hint is gone: the tab has rows, so no empty
# state at all.
expect screen lacks "not live yet"
